Afterbird: allow unpacked extensions without the developer-mode toggle.

M151 gates unpacked extensions behind the `kExtensionsUIDeveloperMode` pref
(extensions_features::kExtensionDisableUnsupportedDeveloper). Anything loaded
via --load-extension or Afterbird's Load Unpacked picker is admitted, then
immediately disabled with DISABLE_UNSUPPORTED_DEVELOPER_EXTENSION: the
extension appears in chrome://extensions but registers no listeners and
filters nothing. On desktop the user flips the toggle in the extensions page;
Afterbird treats sideloading as a first-class flow, so the check is dropped.

Store-installed extensions are unaffected — their location is not kUnpacked,
so this predicate already returned true for them.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/extensions/extension_management.cc b/chrome/browser/extensions/extension_management.cc
index 0000000000..0000000001 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/extensions/extension_management.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/extensions/extension_management.cc
@@ -398,6 +398,10 @@ bool ExtensionManagement::IsAllowedByUnpublishedAvailabilityPolicy(

 bool ExtensionManagement::IsAllowedByUnpackedDeveloperModePolicy(
     const Extension& extension) {
+  // Afterbird: sideloading (--load-extension / Load Unpacked) is a supported
+  // flow, so unpacked extensions are not gated behind the developer-mode
+  // pref the desktop UI exposes.
+  return true;
   if (!base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(
           extensions_features::kExtensionDisableUnsupportedDeveloper)) {
     return true;
